{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PujMdpA7nB5npV9WQXsZcv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Claude tokenizer Korean token ratio English comparison\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/claudeguide/korean-vs-english-do-you-pay-more-tokens-for-the-same-prompt-jm8\"},{\"title\":\"which llm is cheapest for your language tokenizer costs measured 1k5m\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/synthorai/which-llm-is-cheapest-for-your-language-tokenizer-costs-measured-1k5m\"},{\"title\":\"26401 feature request non english users korean japanese cjk face structural disadvanta\",\"url\":\"https://claudeissues.com/issue/26401-feature-request-non-english-users-korean-japanese-cjk-face-structural-disadvanta\"},{\"title\":\"Björn Plüster\",\"url\":\"https://de.linkedin.com/in/bj%C3%B6rn\"},{\"title\":\"The Non-English Token Tax — Korean Costs 1.4x, Measured\",\"url\":\"https://jangwook.net/en/blog/en/multilingual-llm-token-tax-experiment/\"},{\"title\":\"Korean Penalty of Large Language Models Derived by the Tokenizer ICICPE 2024\",\"url\":\"https://hiai.korea.ac.kr/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Korean-Penalty-of-Large-Language-Models-Derived-by-the-Tokenizer_ICICPE_2024.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"LLM literacy series · 01 of 07\",\"url\":\"https://stat.unm.edu/~ronald/ALFF/tokenization_explorer.html\"},{\"title\":\"concepts.dsebastien.net\",\"url\":\"https://concepts.dsebastien.net/concept/token/\"},{\"title\":\"tokenization visualizer\",\"url\":\"https://blakecrosley.com/blog/tokenization-visualizer\"}]\n\nThe sources disagree widely on the Korean-to-English token ratio for Claude, and most don't measure Claude's own tokenizer directly.\n\n- **About 1.3x (measured with a different tokenizer):** One developer write-up measured eight meaning-matched Korean/English pairs and found a mean of 1.30x, with a range of 1.09x to 1.42x. Measured across 8 meaning-matched Korean/English pairs with the o200k_base BPE tokenizer, the mean ratio was 1.30x (median 1.33x, range 1.09x to 1.42x). That work used OpenAI's o200k_base, not Claude's tokenizer. The author argues the ratio is roughly similar across tokenizers, but that is an assumption, not something they tested against Claude.\n\n- **About 1.4x on Claude's tokenizer:** A blog post compared Korean, Japanese, English, and Chinese versions of the same 285 articles across three tokenizers, including Claude's, using the Xenova/claude-tokenizer port. The headline figure is Korean at about 1.4x English, but the Claude totals in the excerpt I could see were cut off, so I could not confirm the exact Claude number.\n\n- **About 2.8x (unclear method):** One blog states that every Korean translation costs approximately 2.8x the English equivalent. The post does not clearly explain how that figure was derived, so treat it with caution.\n\n- **Anecdotal 2–3x:** A GitHub feature request gives a small table of informal examples and concludes that Korean users consume roughly 2x–3x more tokens to communicate the same information. The figures are approximate and the method is not described.\n\n- **Academic work:** A Korean paper (ICICPE 2024) defines a \"Korean penalty\" as the ratio of Korean to English burden and tests tokenizers on the FLORES-200 parallel corpus. Experimental results indicate a linear increase in the disadvantage faced by Korean text as the Korean/English character length ratio rises. The excerpt I saw did not give Claude-specific numbers.\n\n- **Per-character view:** One comparison reports that on Claude, Korean runs about 106 net tokens per 100 characters, against about 32 tokens per 100 characters for English. That is a per-character measure, not a per-meaning ratio, so it isn't directly comparable to the figures above. The same source notes that Claude Fable 5, Opus 4.8, and Sonnet 5 share one tokenizer, and that Claude is not the leanest tokenizer for Korean. A separate source says GPT-5.5 is leanest for Korean.\n\n**Bottom line:** Most credible estimates put Korean at roughly 1.3x to 1.4x the English token count for the same content, with informal claims of 2x to 3x. The range depends on the text type and the tokenizer, and I found no official Anthropic figure. To get a number for your own content, count tokens with Anthropic's token-counting tool or API on matched English and Korean text.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c1496c7-a380-4fcf-a5c2-7d2accf0fc54","uuid":"66b54941-c675-452e-b046-981187e9a758","timestamp":"2026-10-18T10:47:28.086Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Claude tokenizer Korean token ratio English comparison","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01R3ipjEKQe3BDnn9LqXAUhv","content":[{"title":"DEV Community","url":"https://dev.to/claudeguide/korean-vs-english-do-you-pay-more-tokens-for-the-same-prompt-jm8"},{"title":"which llm is cheapest for your language tokenizer costs measured 1k5m","url":"https://dev.to/synthorai/which-llm-is-cheapest-for-your-language-tokenizer-costs-measured-1k5m"},{"title":"26401 feature request non english users korean japanese cjk face structural disadvanta","url":"https://claudeissues.com/issue/26401-feature-request-non-english-users-korean-japanese-cjk-face-structural-disadvanta"},{"title":"Björn Plüster","url":"https://de.linkedin.com/in/bj%C3%B6rn"},{"title":"The Non-English Token Tax — Korean Costs 1.4x, Measured","url":"https://jangwook.net/en/blog/en/multilingual-llm-token-tax-experiment/"},{"title":"Korean Penalty of Large Language Models Derived by the Tokenizer ICICPE 2024","url":"https://hiai.korea.ac.kr/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Korean-Penalty-of-Large-Language-Models-Derived-by-the-Tokenizer_ICICPE_2024.pdf"},{"title":"LLM literacy series · 01 of 07","url":"https://stat.unm.edu/~ronald/ALFF/tokenization_explorer.html"},{"title":"concepts.dsebastien.net","url":"https://concepts.dsebastien.net/concept/token/"},{"t